ExpressiveOS vendor config
==========================

This is `vendor/lineage` for ExpressiveOS, an Android 17 ROM for Google Pixel
phones built on LineageOS 24.0. It is based on LineageOS's own
[vendor/lineage](https://github.com/LineageOS/android_vendor_lineage) and keeps
its layout and its `lineage_<device>` product names. On top of LineageOS's
config it carries what every ExpressiveOS phone shares:

* `config/`: the product configuration each device tree inherits (common
  packages, properties, version and build type).
* `build/`: the build environment (`build/envsetup.sh`, which the tree's
  `build/envsetup.sh` sources) and the build tasks, among them the OTA package
  and the target-files zip it is made from.
* `overlay/`: resource overlays for the framework and apps, including the
  default wallpaper.
* `prebuilt/`, `bootanimation/`, `audio/`: files copied into the images.

Getting the source
------------------

ExpressiveOS's [manifest](https://github.com/ExpressiveOS/manifest) lists every
project, so no local manifests are needed:

    repo init -u https://github.com/ExpressiveOS/manifest -b expressiveos --git-lfs
    repo sync -c -j4 --no-clone-bundle --no-tags

Building
--------

ExpressiveOS is built with its build kit, which sets up the tree, adds
ExpressiveOS's boot animation and wallpapers, and makes, checks and signs each
build. The manifest's README says where the kit is and how to run it.

A product that installs `bootanimation.zip` must set `TARGET_BOOTANIMATION`:
this tree has no default boot animation, and the build stops without one.

